# Example 22: Pattern synthesis - programmable morphogenesis
# Programmable cells move, secrete a diffusible morphogen (AI-2) and
# deposit pigment, turning the population into a self-organizing
# pattern generator.  The founder cluster disperses into a radially
# expanding disk under the "force" mechanics while the AI-2 field marks
# the colony's metabolic footprint with a central hotspot - the
# activator-inhibitor motifs behind Turing's chemical patterns
# (Turing 1952, DOI:10.1098/rstb.1952.0012; Murray, *Mathematical
# Biology*; Kondo & Miura 2010, DOI:10.1126/science.1182967).
#
# Molecular logic:
#   - a constitutive "signal" gene (OP_SIGNAL) secretes AI-2 into the
#     shared field, which diffuses with the population's signal_diffusion
#   - a constitutive "pigment" gene (OP_BUILD_PIGMENT) colors the cell,
#     so the colony extent reads as a pigment map
#   - the "force" mechanics pushes every cell toward the least-crowded
#     neighbor (spatial cell-cell repulsion), turning one dense founder
#     cluster into a patterned 2D structure instead of a single pile
#   - the morphogen gradient created by the dispersing colony is the
#     template on which denser/larger colonies grow spot and stripe
#     motifs (long-range inhibition by the diffusing signal)
#
# The intracellular program is declared below; the Python API runs the
# multicellular morphogenesis.

#promoter name=p_sig strength=-0.4         # constitutive signaler
#promoter name=p_pig strength=-0.4         # constitutive pigment

#gene name=signaler promoter=p_sig
ATG TCA TAA
#end

#gene name=pigment promoter=p_pig
ATG TGG TAA
#end

#regulate p_sig -> signaler strength=+0.8
#regulate p_pig -> pigment strength=+0.9

